  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: The RNA encoder is the most impactful design axis so far — switching from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 in the multiprofile RNA-only setting improved accuracy from 0.591 to 0.650 (+0.06), the largest single-factor gain observed. However, scgpt has not been tested at all, leaving a major uncertainty about whether a third, potentially stronger RNA representation exists. Question: config_008 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_005 (same settings but scvi_n200), isolating the effect of the RNA encoder. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It directly tests the most consequential unexplored axis before committing budget to multimodal or image-encoder variants built on top of it. (2) If scgpt matches or exceeds scvi, it reopens the multimodal search with a stronger RNA backbone; if it underperforms, we can confidently focus remaining budget on scvi-based configurations. (3) It changes only one factor relative to config_005, avoiding the confound of simultaneously altering encoder, modality, or aggregation. This maximizes information gained per experiment under the limited budget."
}

